ums averaging $51 a month in 2027, up from $34. See what to compare before open enrollment ends December 7.","generator":"Astro v4.16.19","og:description":"KFF projects stand-alone Medicare Part D premiums averaging $51 a month in 2027, up from $34. See what to compare before open enrollment ends December 7.","og:image":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon-192.png","og:site_name":"ModernWallet","og:title":"Medicare Part D 2027: KFF Projects Premiums Up 50%","og:type":"website","og:url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/medicare-part-d-2027-premiums/","twitter:card":"summary_large_image","twitter:description":"KFF projects stand-alone Medicare Part D premiums averaging $51 a month in 2027, up from $34. See what to compare before open enrollment ends December 7.","twitter:image":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon-192.png","twitter:title":"Medicare Part D 2027: KFF Projects Premiums Up 50%","viewport":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},"schema":[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@id":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/#organization","@type":"Organization","description":"Free, accurate financial calculators — auto loans, mortgages, retirement, investing, rentals, and net worth. No signup, instant results.","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/favicon.svg"},"name":"ModernWallet","parentOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Layer3Labs","url":"https://www.layer3labs.io"},"url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@id":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/#website","@type":"WebSite","description":"Free, accurate financial calculators — auto loans, mortgages, retirement, investing, rentals, and net worth. No signup, instant results.","name":"ModernWallet","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/","name":"ModernWallet","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/","name":"Guides","position":2},{"@type":"ListItem","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/guides/medicare-part-d-2027-premiums/","name":"Medicare Part D 2027 Stand-Alone Plan Premiums Projected to Rise 50 Percent","position":3}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"KFF projects the average stand-alone Part D premium at $51 a month in 2027, up from $34, if enrollees keep their current plans. That works out to $612 a year, or $204 more than 2026, by arithmetic. Individual premiums vary by plan, and Medicare.gov lists the maximum 2027 deductible as $700."},"name":"How much will Part D cost in 2027?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. CMS sets a 2027 base beneficiary premium of $41.33. KFF lists eight national stand-alone plans with projected 2027 premiums, and Medicare.gov publishes 2027 deductible and out-of-pocket limits. What KFF reports is that no zero-premium stand-alone plans are available in 2027."},"name":"Is Medicare Part D going away in 2027?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"KFF projects the average stand-alone premium will rise 50 percent, from $34 to $51 a month, if enrollees do not switch plans. CMS says it will end the voluntary premium stabilization demonstration for stand-alone plans at the end of 2026 and sets the 2027 base beneficiary premium at $41.33. KFF's release does not say why plans raised premiums."},"name":"What do KFF and CMS say about the 2027 increase?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"KFF says open enrollment runs through December 7. Plans can be compared before then in Medicare Plan Finder at medicare.gov/plan-compare."},"name":"When does Medicare open enrollment end?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The maximum Part D deductible in 2027 is $700, up from $615 in 2026, and some plans charge less or nothing. KFF puts the average at $643 for stand-alone plan enrollees and $489 for MA-PD enrollees. After the deductible, Medicare.gov says enrollees pay 25 percent coinsurance until out-of-pocket spending reaches $2,400."},"name":"What is the Part D deductible in 2027?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Medicare.gov's Extra Help page lists the 2027 plan premium and deductible as $0 for people in the program. Generic drugs cost up to $5.80 and brand-name drugs up to $14.40 at participating pharmacies, and covered drugs cost $0 once total drug costs reach $2,400. Medicare.gov says applications go through Social Security."},"name":"Does Extra Help lower Part D premiums?"}]},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Person","description":"Jonathan Velez writes and edits ModernWallet's personal-finance content, focused on loans, interest, and debt payoff. Every calculator page is reviewed against primary sources like the CFPB and Federal Reserve.","jobTitle":"Personal Finance Writer & Editor","knowsAbout":["Auto loans","Loan amortization","Interest and APR","Debt payoff strategies","Personal finance"],"name":"Jonathan Velez","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/about/","worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ModernWallet","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com"}},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jonathan Velez","url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/about/"},"citation":[{"@type":"CreativeWork","name":"KFF: Average monthly premium for Medicare Part D stand-alone plans projected to increase 50% in 2027","url":"https://www.kff.org/medicare/the-average-monthly-premium-for-medicare-part-d-stand-alone-plans-is-projected-to-increase-by-50-from-34-to-51-in-2027-unless-enrollees-switch-to-lower-cost-plans/"},{"@type":"CreativeWork","name":"CMS: Medicare Part D 2027 national average monthly bid amount information","url":"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/medicar